    "Round v2 used an add_box bed. add_box is a volumetric grid-node velocity overwrite with no normal support; its own docstring points to add_sdf_collider for surface contact. The channel fell into its own bed, ~32000 re-entries per frame, and every number from that round is void.",
    "Round v3 (SDF bed, no sustained head) is in the right regime but its discharge decays from 0.28 to 0.009 m2/s, so the ratio is swept through rather than held.",
    "Round v4 (SDF bed + head at 0.8 m/s) holds discharge steady but drives the approach SUPERCRITICAL (Fr 1.13 to 1.64), where the Rouse ratio does not apply.",
    "A ratio read off a decaying transient, or off a supercritical approach, is not a validation. Neither round establishes the 1.4x test as passed or failed."
